---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro"
import SectionContainer from "@/components/SectionContainer.astro"
import CaseHeader from "@/components/CaseHeader.astro"
import LinkButton from "@/components/LinkButton.astro"
import GitHub from "@/components/icons/GitHub.astro"
import Link from "@/components/icons/Link.astro"
---

<Layout
  title="Vehimac — workshop ERP | Diego Sarmiento"
  description="Vehimac ERP case study: FastAPI, PostgreSQL, work orders, finances and an API in production for a workshop in Bolivia."
>
  <main class="px-4 py-24">
    <SectionContainer>
      <CaseHeader
        kicker="Backend · case study"
        title="Vehimac — ERP for a workshop in Bolivia"
        summary="An auto repair and 3D printing shop ran on Excel, WhatsApp and parts customers never picked up. I built the backend and data model of a lightweight ERP that is already running in production."
      />

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <LinkButton href="https://github.com/degosenpai211/Vehimac">
          <GitHub class="size-5" />
          Code
        </LinkButton>
        <LinkButton href="https://vehimac-production-9609.up.railway.app/docs">
          <Link class="size-4" />
          OpenAPI /docs
        </LinkButton>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-14 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Problem</h2>
        <p>
          The shop needs to quote over WhatsApp, track every part (design →
          installation), charge in bolivianos and read an income statement
          similar to its Excel sheet. Without a data model, finished orders
          got mixed with delivered ones and the margin was unreadable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          A React PWA on Vercel talks to FastAPI on Railway. FastAPI uses no
          ORM: it reaches Postgres through PostgREST (Supabase). The SQL lives
          in versioned migrations. Request flow: UI → <code>/api</code> →
          router → service → Postgres.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-3 text-sm sm:grid-cols-4">
          {
            [
              ["React PWA", "Kanban, finances, PDF quotes"],
              ["FastAPI", "Routers, schemas, services"],
              ["PostgreSQL", "10 tables and 16 migrations"],
              ["Railway + Vercel", "API and frontend in production"],
            ].map(([name, detail]) => (
              <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
                <p class="font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">{name}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">{detail}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          API modules: <code>clients</code>, <code>mechanics</code>,
          <code>work-orders</code>, <code>proformas</code>,
          <code>stored-pieces</code>, <code>finances</code>,
          <code>dashboard</code>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Decisions</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Kanban without N+1:</strong> every
            <code>.execute()</code> against Supabase is a network round trip.
            The order list no longer fetches parts one by one.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Process in JSONB:</strong> 5
            fixed steps per part (migration v11) instead of a steps table the
            shop was never going to maintain.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Prospect ≠ client:</strong> a
            quote only needs a name and a WhatsApp number; the prospect becomes
            a client only when they accept or the quote turns into a work
            order. Otherwise it is deleted after 7 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Deferred auth:</strong> today
            anyone with the URL can operate. It is an explicit debt for when
            the API moves to a VPS with native Postgres.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Data model</h2>
        <p>
          Tables: <code>clients</code>, <code>vehicles</code>,
          <code>mechanics</code>, <code>work_orders</code>,
          <code>order_items</code>, <code>order_photos</code>,
          <code>proformas</code>, <code>proforma_items</code>,
          <code>finances</code>, <code>finance_settings</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Work order states: in progress → finished (part ready, customer has
          not picked it up) → delivered (income recorded in finances). That
          business rule is what I later analyze in the data case.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-white">Outcome and limits</h2>
        <p>
          The shop has a KPI panel, QR payments, PDF quotes sent over WhatsApp
          and an income statement by week and by month. The code and
          migrations are on GitHub; the API can be inspected at
          <code>/docs</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          There are no automated tests and no auth. The next documented step
          is a VPS (Nginx, PM2, native Postgres) and login. The operations
          analysis is in the
          <a class="text-yellow-600 dark:text-yellow-200" href="/en/proyectos/analisis-taller">data case</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </SectionContainer>
  </main>
</Layout>
